    "body": "## Overview\n\nSkip redundant `movedim` + `reshape` tensor view operations when `dim=0` in `all_gather` and `reduce_scatter`, the common case for sequence parallelism.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Eliminates 2-3 redundant tensor view operations per `all_gather(dim=0)` call\n- Eliminates 2 redundant `movedim` + `contiguous` calls per `reduce_scatter(dim=0)` call\n- These are on the TP forward pass hot path (2N calls for N-layer models)\n\n## Validation\n\n- `ruff check` and `ruff format --check`: all passed\n- Logic verification: when `dim=0`, `movedim(0, 0)` returns the same tensor (no-op), and `reshape` produces the same shape — skipping them is behavior-preserving\n\n## Details\n\n`all_gather` with `dim=0` performs:\n1. `output_tensor.reshape((world_size,) + input_size)` — creates a view\n2. `output_tensor.movedim(0, 0)` — no-op, returns same tensor\n3. `output_tensor.reshape(output_size)` — same shape as before step 1\n\nAll three are redundant when `dim=0`. Return `output_tensor` directly after `all_gather`.\n\n`reduce_scatter` with `dim=0` performs:\n1. `input_.movedim(0, 0).contiguous()` — movedim is no-op, contiguous returns same tensor if already contiguous\n2. `output.movedim(0, 0).contiguous()` — same\n\nSkip both movedim calls and only call `.contiguous()` on the input (needed for correctness regardless of dim).\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
